<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · artifact</p><h1 class="enc-title">Divine Bell of King Seongdeok</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">771</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a> · Also known as Emille Bell, Bell of King Seongdeok</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Divine Bell of King Seongdeok is a large bronze bell of Silla, begun by King Gyeongdeok in memory of his father Seongdeok and completed in 771 under King Hyegong. It weighs about 19 tonnes and is decorated with flying celestial figures. Also called the Emille Bell, it is a National Treasure of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-korea">South Korea</a> and hangs at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gyeongju">Gyeongju</a> National Museum.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/divine-bell-of-king-seongdeok.jpg" alt="Divine Bell of King Seongdeok" width="320" height="208" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Steve46814 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:National_Museum-Emile_Bell_-_Gyeongju_3781-06.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
